  "analyst_notes": "Twelve named analysts updated NVDA across the Nov 16-23 window covering Q3 FY27 earnings (Nov 17) and Jensen Huang's Nov 22 CEO reinstatement (filed Nov 23): post-Q3 cuts (Morgan Stanley to $260, Jefferies to $250, UBS to $220) gave way on Nov 23 to upgrades and raises (Citi $225 to $240, Melius Hold to Buy $185 to $220, Bernstein Market Perform to Outperform at $200, while BofA reiterated $280, BMO $240, Goldman $220, Baird Hold $200). Five Nov 23 calls carry a documented 12-month horizon via StockAnalysis (plus Baird's prior Finbold note) and produce a $224.00 weighted target (+35.7%), 8.3 pp above our $210.25 base case (+27.4%); the gap reflects roughly 1.0 turn of P/E or ~7% higher FY28 EPS (Street FY28 EPS consensus sits near $15.70-$16.60 vs our $14.50). The seven calls without a documented horizon ($200-$293, including Wedbush $293 and BofA $280) sit slightly higher and remain in the rating mix (11 Buy, 1 Hold), while the 56-analyst Yahoo Finance aggregate averages $244.18.",
